# A pattern with no `**/` matches at the TOP LEVEL ONLY. `node_modules/` therefore excluded
# `/node_modules` and left every workspace's own — `backend/node_modules`,
# `packages/*/node_modules` — in the build context. That is why a local `docker build` on a
# developer machine went green over a Dockerfile CI could not build: the workspace whose
# manifest the image never installed still received the host's installed `node_modules`
# through the source COPY, so its `tsc` found the types the image had not fetched. Every
# build-output and tooling directory below is recursive for the same reason.
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store

**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo

**/coverage
**/.nyc_output

**/.git
.gitignore
.github/

Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

specs/
.specify/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
README.md
docs/
